# Local working data: firmware images, boot-ROM dumps, Ghidra projects, decompilation and disassembly exports, IQ
# captures, external clones. It holds MediaTek's code and what is derived from it, so it never goes into git;
# README.md "Rebuilding work/" says how to recreate it.
work/

# Firmware build outputs (make -C fw): objects, hook images and the patched MediaTek images
fw/build/
fw/out/

# Binaries of any kind: firmware images, memory dumps, IQ captures, register and SRAM snapshots
*.bin
*.npy
*.cs16
*.cf32
*.pcap
# ...except the Rust receiver's synthetic test vectors (generated by tools/nbnode/testdata/gen.py)
!tools/nbnode/testdata/*.cf32

# Python and Rust build caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
tools/nbnode/target/
